          %h1#idea Idea
          %p
            This entry list details on concrete constructions for examples of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+function+theory"} geometric function theories
          %p
            Recall the notion of
            %em geometric function object
            from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+function+theory"} geometric function theory
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Grpd"} ∞-Grpd
            – a
            %em geometric function theory
            is some kind of assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C : \mathbf{H} \to (\infty,1)Cat
          %p
            such that for
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
            the object
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X)
            behaves to some useful extent like a collection of “functions on
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            More concretely, this will usually be taken to mean that
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            satisfies properties of the following kind:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong existence of pull-push
                – For every morphism
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
                in
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                there is naturally (functorially) an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ←
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* : C(A) \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} C(B) : f^*
                with
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
                playing the role of push-forward of functions along
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                and
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
