                  %mo ≃
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C(X \times_Z Y) \simeq C(X) \times_{C(Z)} C(Y)
          %h3#remarks remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                This is – more or less implicitly – the notion of geometric ∞-functions that underlies
                = succeed "\u2018" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoidification"} groupoidification
                as well as the generalized sections that appear at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Nonabelian+cocycles+and+their+sigma+model+QFTs"} these sigma-model notes
            %li
              %p
                The definition seems to be disturbingly non-linearized, but this should be viewed in light of the possible nature of the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_62.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = E
                is, for instance, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
                incarnation of the total space of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                associated to a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_63.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
                %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_64.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                picks a bunch of vectors in that bundle, hence picks a “distributional section” of that bundle.
          %h2#undercategories_of_quantities
            under-categories of
            = succeed "-quantities" do
              %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_65.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            By essentially simply applying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
            for the case that the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            to the above example one obtains the following example.
          .standout
            %p Tentative.
          %p
            Recall the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-quantity"} ∞-quantity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models+for+%E2%88%9E-stack+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} models for ∞-stack (∞,1)-toposes
            every object
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_66.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathbf{H}
            may be modeled as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_67.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(-)
            be the map that sends simplicial presheaves to cosimplicial copresheaves as described at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-quantity"} ∞-quantity
          %p Then consider the assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_113c989f2e9b2a0f6487505e924b173522c83f79_68.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
